  {
   "id": "UOkam8IZjDQJ",
   "from": "Bob Carpenter",
   "author": "8aa9b8cc06fdc99c",
   "date": "2013-12-23T18:52:16Z",
   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] Parse error for variables starting with \"inf\" or \"nan\"",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "That&#39;s indeed a bug.  Thanks for the report.  I&#39;ll look\r<br>into trying to fix the underlying issue, which is that it&#39;s\r<br>trying to parse an expression, which can be a number,\r<br>and the parser&#39;s peeling the &quot;inf&quot; off the front as a number.\r<br>That&#39;s why you see the error at the location you do.\r<br>\r<br>I amended our issue to make sure we fix the issue you bring up:\r<br>\r<br>   <a href=\"https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/issues/239\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/issues/239&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467273517000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0rTX9Q3ekh0b4dnkw5lA91\">https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/issues/239</a>\r<br>\r<br>- Bob\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>On 12/23/13, 7:32 AM, Gabriel McManus wrote:\r<br>&gt; Attached is an example file that has a data variable called &quot;inftest&quot;. It produces the below parse error. A similar\r<br>&gt; error is produced if the variable is called &quot;nantest&quot;. If it is called just &quot;test&quot; the file compiles fine.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; &quot;inf&quot; and &quot;nan&quot; are reserved words, but shouldn&#39;t it be possible to have a variable that starts with these strings?\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt;  &gt; test &lt;- stan(file=&#39;test.stan&#39;, data=list(inftest=0));\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; TRANSLATING MODEL &#39;test&#39; FROM Stan CODE TO C++ CODE NOW.\r<br>&gt; Error in stanc(file = file, model_code = model_code, model_name = model_name,  :\r<br>&gt;    failed to parse Stan model &#39;test&#39; with error message:\r<br>&gt; EXPECTATION FAILURE LOCATION: file=input; line=8, column=19\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;      y ~ normal(inftest, 1);\r<br>&gt;                    ^-- here\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; DIAGNOSTIC(S) FROM PARSER:\r<br>&gt; Parser expecting: &quot;)&quot;\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; This is the R session info:\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt;  &gt; sessionInfo()\r<br>&gt; R version 3.0.2 (2013-09-25)\r<br>&gt; Platform: x86_64-w64-mingw32/x64 (64-bit)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; locale:\r<br>&gt; [1] LC_COLLATE=English_Australia.1252  LC_CTYPE=English_Australia.1252    LC_MONETARY=English_Australia.1252\r<br>&gt; [4] LC_NUMERIC=C                       LC_TIME=English_Australia.1252\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; attached base packages:\r<br>&gt; [1] stats     graphics  grDevices utils     datasets  methods   base\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; other attached packages:\r<br>&gt; [1] rstan_2.0.1   inline_0.3.13 Rcpp_0.10.6\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; loaded via a namespace (and not attached):\r<br>&gt; [1] codetools_0.2-8 stats4_3.0.2    tools_3.0.2\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt;\r<br>"
    ],
    [
